<h1>Time Management for a Working Mom</h1>
<div class="meta">By Loane Carcallas | Family Tips Blog | 5 min read</div>

<p>Women today are not the same as before. Before, a mother could be a full-time housewife. But now that inflation is high, the husband's salary is often not enough.</p>

<p>It's a bonus if the husband has a big salary and you only have one child, then the wife can stay at home. But in other situations, even if there is only one child, there are still wives who want to earn their own money. Some do online selling, some have online jobs, and some have a secular job.</p>

<p>It is nice to hear that women are earning. But it is not easy because there is a challenge: the household. It cannot be avoided that a wife will miss some household responsibilities when she is working.</p>

<h2>The Solution: The 8-8-8 Rule</h2>

<p>To stay productive, here are suggestions on how to manage her time. Divide the day into three 8-hour blocks:</p>

<div class="highlight-box">
  <div class="time-block"><span class="time">8 Hours Sleep</span> <span>Rest and recharge</span></div>
  <div class="time-block"><span class="time">8 Hours Work</span> <span>Secular work</span></div>
  <div class="time-block"><span class="time">8 Hours Life</span> <span>Family, chores, and self</span></div>
</div>

<h2>A Sample Schedule That Works</h2>

<p><strong>9:00 PM - 5:00 AM (Sleep):</strong> If you wake up at 5am to take care of the kids, you should sleep at 9pm.</p>

<p><strong>5:00 AM - 7:00 AM (Morning Chores):</strong> Do basic quick chores like cooking food for breakfast and lunch, cleaning the kitchen, washing dishes, ironing uniforms, sweeping, fixing the bed, and cleaning the CR. By 7am, the mother should have breakfast.</p>

<p><strong>7:00 AM - 9:00 AM (Spiritual):</strong> Spend time studying the scriptures until 9am.</p>

<p><strong>9:00 AM - 11:00 AM (Online Work):</strong> Spend time editing articles, photos, or videos for her online job.</p>

<p><strong>11:00 AM - 1:00 PM (Prep):</strong> Prepare herself to go to work.</p>

<p><strong>1:00 PM - 8:00 PM (Secular Work):</strong> Logged in at work and will go home at 8pm.</p>

<p><strong>8:00 PM - 9:00 PM (Family & Me-Time):</strong> Dinner and me-time for herself, like a beauty routine or quality talks with the family.</p>

<h2>What About Day Off?</h2>

<p>It sounds nice, right? It seems like there is no leisure or grocery or market time, but you can spend that on your day off, like Sunday. Since there is no secular work on Sunday, you can put it in the 1pm to 8pm slot.</p>

<p>No family outing? You can do it on Sunday morning after church. It is still quality time. As long as there is discipline in using time and energy, it will still result in quality time.</p>

<p><em>I hope this article helped a mother, whether she is working or not.</em></p>

